# ⚠️ backend/patches/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
# backend/package.json runs `patch-package` on postinstall, and
# patches/whatsapp-web.js+1.34.7.patch is what keeps a paired WhatsApp session
# from being dropped immediately. When this directory was ignored, postinstall
# silently no-oped on the VPS (it ends in `|| echo "Patch applied or skipped"`)
# and the server ran an unpatched whatsapp-web.js. Verify after cloning:
#     git ls-files backend/patches/
# Any conflict with a local node_modules must be fixed in the patch itself.
# Database snapshots (persisted in Cloudflare R2)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
